        <!-- Workflow -->
        <section id="workflow" class="space-y-4 border-b border-line pb-8 scroll-mt-20">
          <h2 class="text-3xl text-ink">Development loop</h2>
          <p class="text-[15px] text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
            Run the smallest check that covers the change. Formatting and the Python repository checks need no GPU and no
            Gufo build; build only the affected target while iterating.
          </p>

          <div class="code-block">
            <div class="code-block-header"><span>Focused checks</span><span>sh</span></div>
            <pre><code><span class="code-comment"># Formatting, shared with CI; add --fix to apply</span>
nix shell --inputs-from . nixpkgs#clang-tools -c python3 tools/ci/check-format.py

<span class="code-comment"># Build and run one test target</span>
nix develop -c cmake --preset gpu-test
nix develop -c cmake --build --preset gpu-test --target &lt;test-target&gt;
nix develop -c ctest --preset gpu-full -R '^&lt;test-name&gt;$' --output-on-failure

<span class="code-comment"># Documentation-only changes</span>
nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.docs</code></pre>
          </div>

          <p class="text-xs text-ink-3 leading-relaxed">
            Hosted CI runs <code class="text-ink-2">nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.pr</code> on Ubuntu with a
            25-minute limit: formatting, documentation, dependency inventory, server-command checks and the CPU contract
            suite. It does not build ROCm, download weights or run model oracles, so run the GPU checks covering your
            change locally. Do not run full model sweeps, video generation or duplicate suites for routine edits. A
            skip caused by a missing model or device is not a quality pass.
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-paper border border-line space-y-2">
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm">Conventions</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-ink-3 leading-relaxed">
                Google style C++20, two-space indent, 80 columns, sorted includes. clang-tidy runs bugprone, cert,
                clang-analyzer, cppcoreguidelines, misc and performance checks over <code class="text-ink-2">src/</code>
                with warnings as errors. One canonical long option and backend name per behavior; no aliases.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-paper border border-line space-y-2">
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm">Evidence, then promotion</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-ink-3 leading-relaxed">
                An optimization changes one mechanism at a time against a trusted oracle, and candidates that lose
                focused correctness or measured performance are rejected. Successful optimizations become the default
                path, without extra switches, and production paths retain quality.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-paper border border-line space-y-2">
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm">Submitting changes</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-ink-3 leading-relaxed">
                Conventional Commits with a single-line message; pull request titles follow the release policy, and the
                squash merge keeps the title on <code class="text-ink-2">main</code>. Version and changelog updates
                are left to the release workflow. Prefer <code class="text-ink-2">jj</code> when available, otherwise
                Git.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Profiling -->
        <section id="profiling" class="space-y-4 border-b border-line pb-8 scroll-mt-20">
          <h2 class="text-3xl text-ink">Profiling and benchmarking</h2>
